# Baked into any production build (both `npm run build` and `npm run build:web`).
#
# This is an ORIGIN — no trailing /api, no trailing slash. src/api.ts appends /api
# for API calls and uses the bare origin for /uploads and the Socket.io connection,
# so a /api suffix here would produce /api/api/... and 404 everything.
#
# The hosted site and the API sit on different domains, so every request is
# cross-origin: the backend's ALLOWED_ORIGINS must list the site's URL, or the
# browser blocks the calls at CORS before they ever reach the server.
#
# The .exe ignores this — Electron injects its own URL on window.HERITAGE at
# runtime, which takes precedence. It is only a fallback there.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://heritage-hospital-1.onrender.com
